I don't know if this is _the_ fix (since I haven't tried it), but perusing
tetris.h will show you

char high_user[15][8];

which is clearly wrong--if this is to hold strings of length 8, it must be
char high_user[15][9];
(to account for the trailing null).  Note that the bug only happens with 8
character user names.
